# This machine has iCloud "Desktop & Documents" sync enabled, so everything under
# ~/Documents — including this repo — is synced to iCloud Drive. iCloud evicts
# cold files, and every read of an evicted file blocks while `bird` re-downloads
# it. That made the toolchain unusable: individual .d.ts reads inside the `next`
# package were timing out at ~8.8s each, `tsc --noEmit` never completed in 20+
# minutes, and concurrent reads failed outright with ECANCELED.
#
# The fix is to keep package *content* out of the synced tree. pnpm stores all
# real files in its virtual store (normally node_modules/.pnpm); pointing that
# outside ~/Documents leaves only tiny symlinks in the repo, which iCloud can
# sync harmlessly. `node_modules` itself must stay a real directory here — pnpm
# refuses to install into a symlinked node_modules root (ENOTDIR).
#
# The store must stay INSIDE the project directory: Turbopack refuses to compile
# packages whose real path resolves outside the project root ("files outside of
# the project directory will not be compiled"), so pointing this at a path under
# $HOME breaks `next build`. A dot-directory ending in `.nosync` satisfies both
# constraints at once — inside the project for Turbopack, ignored by iCloud.
#
# If this repo ever moves outside ~/Documents, or Desktop & Documents sync is
# turned off, this file can be deleted and `pnpm install` re-run.
virtual-store-dir=.pnpm.nosync
